QUERY set_file_prop -h
Brief:
  Set file's properties.
Usage:
  set_file_prop [options] <file...>
Arguments:
  <file...>  The files being set.
Options:
  -h, --help      Show this help.
  -lib <library>  Specifies the library associated with VHDL files.
                  Multiple libraries must be separated by comma and
                  included in a pair of braces.


QUERY import_files -h
Brief:
  Import files.
Usage:
  import_files [options]
Options:
  -h, --help            Show this help.
  -file <ValueList>     Import file to current project.e.g. -file fileA
                        fileB
  -dir <dir>            Import folder to current project.
                        e.g. -dir /user/src
  -fileList <fileList>  Import the file list base on the given file.
                        e.g. -fileList importList.txt
  -force                Cover if file exist.
                        e.g. -force


QUERY add_file -h
Brief:
  Add design files.
Usage:
  add_file [options] <file...>
Arguments:
  <file...>  The files being added.
Options:
  -h, --help    Show this help.
  -type <type>  Override file type explicitly. This command automatically
                judge the file's type by it extension name. This option
                can override it.
  -disable      Add but disable the file.


QUERY create_project -h
Brief:
  Create project.
Usage:
  create_project [options]
Options:
  -h, --help                        Show this help.
  -name <name>                      Specify the project name.e.g. -name
                                    fpga_project
  -dir <dir>                        Specify the create path.
                                    e.g. -dir /user/project
  -pn <part_number>                 Specify the device part number.
                                    e.g. -pn GW1N-UV4LQ144C6/I5
  -device_version <device_version>  Specify the device version.
                                    e.g. -device_version NA|B|C|D
  -force                            Cover if project exist.
                                    e.g. -force


QUERY open_project -h
Brief:
  Open a project file(.gprj).
Usage:
  open_project [options] <file>
Arguments:
  <file>  Project file to be read.
Options:
  -h, --help                        Show this help.
  -pn <part_number>                 Open the project using this
                                    part(overrides project's part)
  -device_version <device_version>  Specify the device version.
                                    e.g. -device_version NA|B|C|D


QUERY set_file_enable -h
Brief:
  Enable/Disable some file in current project.
Usage:
  set_file_enable [options] <file> <true|false>
Arguments:
  <file>        The file being set.
  <true|false>  true for enable, false for disable
Options:
  -h, --help  Show this help.


